/athletes/60354"} "İsmail Oğan"] " and threw Pakistani " [:a {:href "/athletes/59561"} "Muhammad Bashir"] " to win the gold medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Blubaugh should have been better known, having won two AAU titles, an NCAA title, and the 1959 Pan American Championships. Habibi went on to win the 1961 and 1962 World Championships and his loss in Roma was his only one ever at a major international. Oğan came back in 1964 and won the gold medal in this class."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60578"} "Doug Blubaugh"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60354"} "İsmail Oğan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TUR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TUR.png"}] "TUR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59561"} "Muhammad Bashir"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/PAK"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/PAK.png"}] "PAK"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58911"} "Gaetano Devescovi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes